{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of distinct ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> have positive integral values satisfying the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/52602a884cb47db7d915d6e63ad91958e835032f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4y^4-10x^2y^2+9=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16e30c870423344ca022fb9a30145575fd85d52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 0\\quad \\text{(B) } 3\\quad \\text{(C) } 4\\quad \\text{(D) } 12\\quad \\text{(E) } \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0283afe7bc2adbc19eea24e8d67e41425e92ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(xy)^2=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" />. The expression given is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a459490c3144b54b5c2865df99c324fde9cf12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-10a+9=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, which can be factored as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8270a751b4292f1f1c9fff15539b3b43caab50ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-9)(a-1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b77838d13ad5eee865086cf74ab277cde3d0518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=(xy)^2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d2241b2adbb372b176f31c58172073a7fde5ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=(xy)^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive, we can eliminate the possibilities where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> is negative. From here it is easy to see that the only integral pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e74a1f07aa0f26c88d72bac2796008fe7e7559e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1), (1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME\" title=\"1969 AHSME\">1969 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1969 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1969\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a 